Force the pure-Python protobuf implementation in the vendored copy.

Upstream probes for the upb/cpp C extensions with importlib.import_module("google._upb._message")
and friends, which imports the application's protobuf by its top-level name (and then warns that
the vendored upb is unavailable), and honours PROTOCOL_BUFFERS_PYTHON_IMPLEMENTATION, which is meant
for the application's protobuf: "cpp" makes descriptor.py import the missing vendored pyext and
crash. Only the pure-Python implementation is vendored, so select it unconditionally.

diff --git a/google/protobuf/internal/api_implementation.py b/google/protobuf/internal/api_implementation.py
--- a/google/protobuf/internal/api_implementation.py
+++ b/google/protobuf/internal/api_implementation.py
@@ -6,7 +6,6 @@
